 boards/<name>/index.html. Rows are grouped into sections by the "section" field and ordered by the earliest date
 in each section; sections whose date has passed go under one fold at the bottom.
+
+A board.json with a "due" entry ({"field": ..., "who": ..., "until": "Thu"}) is a task list instead: rows go into
+"Nobody on it yet", "Overdue", "Due by <next until-day>" and "Later" by their due date as of the day the page is
+built, and done rows go under one fold. An optional "rota" entry ({"title", "data", "date", "who"}) adds a weekly
+rota at the top, from this week on.
